From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 00:15:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: dwc: Fix stray newline in the no-fixup notice

dw_pcie_parent_bus_offset() logs a note when a platform that once had a
cpu_addr_fixup() turns out not to need one. The format string breaks the
line before the semicolon, so the one message is emitted as two records
and the second carries no device prefix:

  imx6q-pcie 33800000.pcie: config reg[1] 0x1ff00000 == cpu 0x1ff00000
  ; no fixup was ever needed for this devicetree

The three sibling messages in the same function all keep the "; " inline
and end with a single newline. Do the same here.

Signed-off-by: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware.c
index ec4722e..a6b7d04 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware.c
@@ -1358,7 +1358,7 @@ resource_size_t dw_pcie_parent_bus_offset(struct dw_pcie *pci,
 		 * Log a note if devicetree didn't describe a translation.
 		 */
 		if (reg_addr == cpu_phys_addr)
-			dev_info(dev, "%s reg[%d] %#010llx == cpu %#010llx\n; no fixup was ever needed for this devicetree\n",
+			dev_info(dev, "%s reg[%d] %#010llx == cpu %#010llx; no fixup was ever needed for this devicetree\n",
 				 reg_name, index, reg_addr,
 				 (unsigned long long) cpu_phys_addr);
 	} else {
-- 
2.47.1

